+English | [中文](2026-11-18-provider-recovery-receipts.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Adds optional recovered-response receipts to assistant/message and optional resolved effort, replay association, and recovery receipt to compaction/summary.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-11-18-provider-recovery-receipts
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:assistant/message"
+    previous: "2026-09-16-session-format-v4"
+    after: "6f158a795f2c5b6624b7c06a1cdebd18c7f65912ba425fa77fb68f5dedba3638"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:compaction/summary"
+    previous: "2026-09-16-session-format-v4"
+    after: "180a7f0870d63d8b44d88e0bc38ccff5da4ae31471801ff748bbce6c49583cf0"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+Existing V4 logs remain valid: every new field is optional and absence never proves recovery approval or durable acknowledgement. New readers continue to derive ordinary assistant content and compaction replacement from the existing required fields. Older readers ignore the optional metadata and can still display/replay content, but do not implement the new recovery APIs; the provider plugin requires explicit host capability markers and fails closed without them. A same-version extension is appropriate because no existing discriminator, payload meaning, or replay rule changes. Recovery identity only authorizes idempotent lookup after a separate current policy check.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+The 19 focused AgentLoop, recovery, request-error, tool-call, initiator, BasicCompaction, manual-compaction, and LLM test files passed 512 tests. Recovery tests use the real JSONL persistence backend and native write lease; a flush callback without a readable backend is refused. They cover idempotent tool adoption, ordinary lost-ACK commits, changed request bodies, unchanged source ranges, cancellation, durable settlement failure, resolved summary effort, route policy, and validated pressure budgets. The affected source projects and focused test TypeScript check passed, as did changed-file lint and public API documentation checks.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
