index c8d0c6b748..c9c8cd3fbf 100644
--- a/packages/compaction/compaction-basic/README.md
+++ b/packages/compaction/compaction-basic/README.md
@@ -97,6 +97,14 @@ With `dsh-command-compact` mounted, type `/compact` in a chat UI to condense imm
 
 Mount `dsh-compaction-tool-result-pruner` before this package to trim oversized tool results as part of condensation. Trimming makes no model call and can remove the need to summarize at all: when the trimmed conversation fits within the threshold, condensation skips the summary. Trimming only runs after a condensation trigger qualifies — a below-pressure conversation is never touched.
 
+### Provider summary policy and captured summaries
+
+`compaction/pressure-policy` supplies optional route-specific overrides for pressure headroom, retention, and summary output budget. Returned fields are merged over the configured target policy and checked with the same strict validator. An explicit retention form replaces the other default form. Unhandled targets retain their defaults; adapters with small local windows can admit a feasible budget without changing unrelated providers.
+
+`compaction/summary-route` can explicitly select the auxiliary provider, model, effort, and output cap. Its version 2 capability supplies `configuredTarget` only when the backend explicitly configures a summary provider/model; `defaultTarget` is that target or the inherited answered-model route. The proposed main-call target remains separate, so provider policies can preserve an explicit summary choice while applying their defaults after a main-model switch. Automatic pre-step, model-switch, and manual entry points preserve that captured proposal. Without a policy override, the answered-model selection described above remains the default. The optional resolved-call observer on `llm.stream()` captures the actual bound route after existing stream middleware; `compaction/summary` records its resolved effort, output cap, usage, and optional replay association.
+
+`compaction/committed` is independent of assistant-message acknowledgement. It runs after the summary, replacement surface, and clean closing event are committed and a flush completes; external providers must require its `durable` flag. `ctx.compaction.adoptRecoveredSummary(agent, input, signal)` requires a summary-specific `compaction/recovery-check` listener and an idle maintenance reservation. It requires a readable `sessionPersistence` backend, validates the complete durable history, response digest, original compaction identity, unchanged surface, and exact original summary messages/tools, then reuses the normal balanced-range, shrink, replacement, and durability transaction. It never creates an assistant message or dispatches a new LLM call. A matching original checkpoint or recovery receipt returns the prior transaction without replacing history again. Missing policy, damaged artifacts, changed history, unresolved partial commits, and unavailable persistence stop recovery; the caller retains responsibility for provider identity, domain fences, and permission checks.
+
